            <ArticleTitle>Infrequent cardiac manifestations of sarcoidosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>515-516</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0147-9563(16)30209-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.hrtlng.2016.08.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac sarcoidosis (CS) is found in 2-7% of patients with systemic sarcoidosis (SS). Its diagnosis and treatment is challenging, notwithstanding the poor prognosis and treatment. Hereby, we present a case of systemic sarcoidosis with rare cardiac manifestations of severe mitral incompetence and large coronary aneurysm in a previously healthy woman. She underwent successful mitral valve replacement and coronary artery bypass surgery and was maintained on low dose glucocorticoid therapy.</AbstractText>
